10. MAIN BOSS BATTLE: SHADOW TITAN

Create a real, playable boss fight.

The Titan must have attacks, movement patterns, telegraphed danger zones, health, damage reactions, and multiple phases.

The fight should be challenging but fair.

The player must be able to defeat the boss through movement, timing, and attacks.

Combat Controls

Desktop:

- WASD or Arrow Keys: Move.
- Space or J: Attack.
- Shift: Dodge or dash.
- E or Enter: Interact.
- Escape: Pause.

Mobile:

- Virtual directional joystick or directional buttons.
- Attack button.
- Dodge button.
- Interact button when appropriate.

Make controls configurable where practical.

Boss Health

Display a large boss health bar near the top of the screen.

The health bar must update when the Titan takes damage.

The boss must have clear damage reactions.

Examples:

- Brief flashing.
- Knockback from appropriate attacks.
- A short stagger animation.
- A sound effect when a successful hit lands.

Avoid allowing the player to defeat the Titan instantly.

Phase 1: Heavy Stomps

The Titan slowly approaches Ain.

It raises one foot before stomping.

Show a warning circle on the ground.

After a short delay, the Titan stomps.

The impact causes an area-of-effect shockwave.

The player must dodge outside the danger zone.

The Titan occasionally swings an arm across the ground.

The player can attack when the Titan finishes its moves.

Phase 2: Purple Energy Attacks

At approximately 65% health, the Titan becomes more aggressive.

Purple energy gathers around its hands.

The Titan launches magical projectiles.

The projectiles should travel toward Ain's position when launched.

The player must move to avoid them.

The Titan can also create a short line of purple energy across the ground.

Display a warning effect before the attack activates.

The player can damage the Titan during recovery windows.

Phase 3: Desperate Rampage

At approximately 30% health, the Titan becomes unstable.

Its purple aura grows brighter.

Its movement becomes faster.

The Titan uses:

- A stronger ground slam.
- A short charging attack.
- A sweeping arm attack.
- A final desperate roar.

Each attack must have readable telegraphs.

Do not make the final phase unfair or unavoidable.

The Titan should become exhausted after its strongest attacks, allowing Ain to retaliate.

The battle should gradually become more emotional as Ain realizes that the monster is still Aidil.

